+    "appearance": "A squat frog-bodied animal with a bulldog’s head, short tail, and oily brown or gray hair. Its front paws are webbed and its rear feet are frog-like. About 2 ft. tall and 50 lb.",
+    "habitats": ["Dream River", "River banks", "Renardy"],
+    "rulesOrigin": "printed-rules-summary",
+    "overridesIndexedRules": true,
+    "preserveIndexedReferences": true,
+    "otherStatistics": "Descending AC 8. THAC0 19. One attack per round. Unsteady morale (5–7). Animal intelligence (1). No magic resistance. Size S, 2 ft. tall. No treasure.",
+    "sections": {
+      "Printed source": "TSR 2524, Savage Coast Monstrous Compendium Appendix, printed pp. 14–15. ",
+      "Attacks": "Bite. One attack for 1d4 damage. It catches small prey with its sticky tongue and pulls the prey to its mouth. The text gives this no separate attack, range, or restraint rule.",
+      "Defenses and Legacy": "Adult batracines have Leap. The p. 8 monster rules allow an instantaneous jump forward or straight upward 20 ft. plus 1 ft. per Hit Die, capped at 35 ft. A 2-HD batracine can jump 22 ft. It uses this to take birds or reach water when threatened. The creature never becomes Afflicted and needs no cinnabryl. It is immune to the amber lotus’s sleep effect. The compendium’s general monster Legacy rules allow three uses per day once fully active and immediate use once activated. The initial week permits one use per day. Its powers fade after leaving the Red Curse and Haze. See printed pp. 6–9.",
+      "Parasites": "Cardinal ticks can infest this creature. If the specimen is infested, a melee encounter leaves the combatants with 5% infestation. Infestation increases by 15 percentage points each time its host attempts to use a Legacy, up to 50% in nonhumanoids. A cinnabryl ointment clears it. Scratching costs 1 HP per percentage point removed unless the special Jibarú medicine is used. See Parasite, printed p. 85.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "Common river carnivore, active at dusk and dawn. Family organization and 1d4 appearing. Adults usually den alone near the Dream River and pair in mating season, with 2–4 pups. They gather to hunt when food is short. They take forest animals and favor birds. Fish and amphibians are outside their diet. Pups sell for 5 gp and a trained pet for 20 gp. The book describes their blood as an ingredient in a potion to counter magical sleep."
+    }
