+      "Attacks": "Three standard attacks, claw/claw/bite for 1d4, 1d4 and 1d8. The table separately lists Forefeet for 1d6 as a special attack. The Combat text says it lashes out with its forefeet in water and uses all four attacks.",
+      "Plant Form Legacy": "After failing a morale check in combat with no apparent way to flee, it takes one round to become a tree. Usually a bald cypress, or a tree suited to its rain forest. The tree is indistinguishable from an ordinary tree, has AC 0, and does not bleed when harmed. Weapon attacks to tree form do at most 1 damage total per round. It stays in tree form up to six hours a day. Plant Form prevents movement, speech and spellcasting under the Campaign Book Legacy rules. It does not need cinnabryl.",
+      "Cover and retreat": "A swampmare has a 30% chance to hide in shadows in thick vegetation. If threatened, it may squeal and flee into water.",
+      "Encounters and ecology": "Uncommon, solitary organization, 3d4 appearing, daytime activity. Gurrash breed domestic strains as mounts and pack animals, each large enough for one gurrash rider. It eats leaves, fruit and other vegetation and needs at least two hours of sunlight daily. Three or more hours in tree form in strong sunlight feed it for a day. Older swampmares spend more time as trees and typically take permanent tree form when they die of old age.",
+      "Source notes": "The printed attack table gives three routine attacks and a separate Forefeet special attack. The combat prose gives four attacks in water without spelling out the individual roll sequence. The 1d6 Forefeet line supplies the damage for the extra attack when applying the water exception."
