+      "Combat": "One attack, 0 direct damage. A trosip attacks only sleepers and stays still whenever someone is awake within the range of its senses. It senses motion and vibration out to 60 ft., including invisible creatures. It moves silently 95% of the time.",
+      "Suffocation": "At least four trosips are needed to attack one man-sized sleeper effectively. The victim saves vs. paralyzation using only magical protection bonuses. A failed save means death from suffocation in 1d4 + 1 rounds. A success wakes the victim in time to wave them away. If more than twelve trosips attack one victim, both of two saving throws must succeed for the victim to survive.",
+      "Detection and retreat": "A stationary trosip looks like ordinary dust. Magic or devices that detect invisible creatures can reveal it, and some animals such as cats can see it. The colony withdraws once the victim wakes or the body begins cooling. The book describes fast short spurts and poor sustained movement.",
