+      "Combat": "One bite for 1d3 damage. Voats can bite on land or in water. They attack small domestic animals and may attack humanoids.",
+      "Disease": "A bite has a 5% chance to transmit a serious disease unless the victim saves vs. poison. The entry gives examples of disease but no onset, duration or further damage.",
+      "Red Curse": "All voats have a Legacy. Most suffer its Affliction and many have Phase. The Phase Affliction gives them soft, distorted flesh and makes them tend to sink into solid matter if they stay in place. They seldom wear cinnabryl and may get trace amounts from scarlet pimpernel.",
+      "Phase Legacy": "If the voat has Phase, it can pass through solid matter for 1 round, up to three times daily once the Legacy is fully active. It can walk without sinking during deliberate phasing. The full effect is immune to solid weapons while phased, but magic missile, the Missile Legacy and magical fire, cold and electricity can still affect it. The Affliction and active Legacy are separate effects.",
+      "Ecology": "Packs raid granaries and ship cargo, gnaw through planks, and foul what they leave. They also nest in caves containing scarlet pimpernels. Nests may hold bright objects and gear from victims. Voats live 2–4 years and typically have 3–5 litters a year of 8–12. Cardinal ticks often infest them, and packs sometimes associate with Saragón lyra birds."
