+      "Printed source": "TSR, Savage Coast Monstrous Compendium Appendix (1996), pp. 117–118.  rule references: Appendix pp. 4, 6–8 and Savage Coast Campaign Book Part 2 pp. 85, 96 and 104 for Class C flight and Legacy procedures. ",
+      "Combat": "When it can rear up, the vulturehound makes three attacks: two front talons for 1d3 each and one beak for 1d4. If it cannot rear, use the beak alone. In flight, it attacks with its front talons. It loses flight after losing more than 75% of starting HP. At exactly 75% loss, it can still fly. Class C movement requires at least half speed, allows a 90-degree turn per round and permits an aerial attack pass every two rounds.",
+      "Red Curse": "Renardy packs acquire Legacies but never suffer Affliction. Yazak Steppes populations lie outside the Red Curse’s direct influence. The text lists Gas Breath, Acid Touch, Gaseous Form and Sleep as common choices. Assign the individual’s Legacy before play.",
+      "Common Legacies": "A fully active Legacy has up to three uses per day. Use the adult’s 2 HD as caster level. Gas Breath lasts up to 2 rounds before expiring and delivers one 1d4 poison hit to a target within 5 ft. Magical poison protection can grant a save vs. poison for half. Acid Touch is instantaneous and deals 1d4 + 2 on a successful hit against plant matter or flesh. Gaseous Form lasts 2 rounds with flight 3 (B), can pass through gaps that are not airtight, and can be driven by normal or magical winds. Most attacks cannot affect it. Magical fire, electricity, magic missile and the Missile Legacy can. Sleep lasts 4 rounds, targets one living creature closest to a location within 10 yards, and allows a save vs. spell.",
+      "Pack and pups": "Packs hunt out of a den and drag back food. Their lair has a 50% chance to hold 3d4 pups. A pup has 1d4 HP, cannot fly, and bites for 1d2 damage. Pups taken young can be trained for war or hunting. A trained adult tracks as a 5th-level ranger or adds +3 to a ranger companion’s tracking skill. Each vulturehound has a 50% chance of cardinal ticks.",
+      "Ecology": "Vulturehounds take carrion and hunt isolated or sick prey. They watch and scent for carrion and bay like dogs. They are immune to vermilia. One animal yields enough blood for 1d6 doses of antivermilia medicine, made by a mage of at least 9th level with an alchemical laboratory. A dose cures a man-sized or smaller creature. The book says doses often cost over 150 gp."
+    }
